This was a strange game, overall. I didn't take many notes because I
was still discouraged from my YASD last week. Still, I learned a lot
from the game, and it was great fun.

I started by doing an XL 2 protection racket. Without the healing
spells and stethoscope of a healer, it's much harder to stay at XL 1,
so I thought it reasonable to gain a level to enable me to rush the
mines a bit more without worrying about dying. I only scraped enough
cash together (via a bit of credit cloning) for one donation, but that
gave me 4 full points of protection.

After this start, my pets started to suffer cruel fates. My first dog
turned into a hell hound (I think from /oP), which was nice, but
somehow managed to end up below minetown and went feral, which wasn't
so nice. A tamed kitten was too big for its boots and died, and after a
couple more pets my fifth pet died of system shock from being polyed.

Quite early on I got crowned making a water prayer. I guess it's best
to break a few mirrors before making a water prayer? Actually, crowning
probably helped my game more than the ability to pray would have, since
by that point I lacked sleep resistance, shock resistance and see
invisible. Having a rustproof weapon which instakills Jabberwocks is
rather nice, too.

The Quest was fun. I attacked the Master of Thieves, who kept hitting
me and teleporting away to heal up, making it very difficult to get his
HP to 0. However, Vorpal Blade cut his head off instead.

My castle wishes were: 2 blessed ?oC (not sure why I did this, I think
I had the PYEC by this point), HoB, GDSM, blessed fireproof robe, 2
attempts at Grayswandir (both of which failed; Vorpal Blade, Demonbane,
Cleaver and PYEC already existed in the game), after which I got the
hint and wished for a magic marker instead.

I wrote up a load of ?oEA and got myself to AC -35ish. I recharged my
wands of death which ran out.

Gehennom went really easily. I was perhaps too well prepared - very
little could actually touch me. None of the demon princes presented any
problem (apart from the possibility of them summoning Demogorgon, which
they didn't). I dug a path from each downstair to each upstair. Killed
Vlad, got the candleabrum, went back to minetown since I'd forgotten
candles (I've never got the candelabrum before!)

At one point I got brainsucked by a master mind flayer. This was just
as I forgot the identify spell, so I lost a few item descriptions.
Nothing too bad, though.

Marked the VS, levelported to the wizard's tower. Killed things until
they were dead. Wand of deathed the WoY. Spent a few turns panicking
because I'd let the Book of the Dead fall in the water. My thought
process went:

"Scrolls of earth! Er, I've got none."
"Reverse genocide giants! Er, none of them either."
"Wand of cold! Nope"
.=2E..
"Spell of cone of cold!"
This last one worked, and I found I didn't even have to dig down to
rescue the book. Grabbed the book, levelported to the VS, performed the
ritual.

Killed things till they were dead. Found myself thankful for all the
insects the priests kept summoning - they were a good barrier from all
the nastier creatures.

Wand of deathed the high priest, grabbed the AoY, legged it.

The mysterious force hit 2 or 3 times, the WoY turned up 2 or 3 times.
I wand of deathed him but I also melee'd him to see if these wand of
death charges were being wasted.

The planes went smooth. Confused gold detection revealed the portals.

On the astral plane, I put my towel on. Famine left, Death middle,
Pestilence right. I went for Famine first. Accidentally hit an Angel of
The Lady with a wand of death.. thereafter, all Angels of The Lady were
hostile - do they start hostile or had I angered them? Wand of deathed
Famine, fought my way to the altar, to find it was chaotic. Quaffed a
potion of full healing, since I was about one-third HP. Started the
slog back to the middle.

Death looked menacing, but the priests summoned enough a to keep him
away from me. I had to go adjacent to him to get through the door to
the middle, but his death touch didn't work. Ran up to the middle
temple, as I entered a nearby vampire fled. This must be it!

Lessons learned:
1) Don't wish for Grayswandir - Vorpal Blade is good enough. Much
better things can be wished for.
2) Keep a handy supply of wands of death.
3) Mind flayers aren't that bad if you deal with them correctly.
4) Same with ;
5) I'm still scared of L though.
6) Polypiling takes too much RL time to be worth it.
7) As soon as you get disintegration resistance, you'll never see
another black dragon again...

